---
/**
 * What Dawnroom and this site do over the network. A plain page: every line follows the code
 * (engine/src/download.rs, custom.rs, runtimes.rs, cli/update.rs, studio/src-tauri/src/updates.rs,
 * site/src/layouts/Base.astro, site/src/lib/fit.ts). Keep it in step when a connection is added.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PRODUCT_NAME, BIN } from '../config';

const connections: { when: string; who: string; host: string; sent: string }[] = [
  {
    when: 'You pull a model, or start your first image',
    who: 'You',
    host: 'huggingface.co and its download servers',
    sent: `The file's address, a resume position, and the name “${BIN}-engine” with its version. No prompts, no hardware details.`,
  },
  {
    when: 'You pull a model, or start your first image, and the image runtime is not installed',
    who: 'You',
    host: 'github.com and its download servers',
    sent: 'The address of the runtime file, and the same program name and version.',
  },
  {
    when: 'You check a Hugging Face link or a custom model in “Add a model”',
    who: 'You',
    host: 'huggingface.co',
    sent: 'The repository you pasted, and a request for the first few kilobytes of its files, to read what kind of model it is.',
  },
  {
    when: 'Studio is open, with “Update automatically” on (the default): about once a day',
    who: 'Studio, on its own',
    host: 'github.com (the latest release’s update list)',
    sent: 'A plain request for the list. Its address has no version, hardware or ID in it. If a newer version is listed, Studio downloads the installer from GitHub and checks its signature.',
  },
  {
    when: `You run ${BIN} update`,
    who: 'You',
    host: 'api.github.com and github.com',
    sent: `The program name and version (“${BIN}-cli”), and the address of the release files.`,
  },
  {
    when: 'You run the install script',
    who: 'You',
    host: 'api.github.com and github.com',
    sent: 'Ordinary requests for the release list and its files.',
  },
  {
    when: 'You run the Windows installer on a PC without WebView2',
    who: 'You',
    host: 'go.microsoft.com',
    sent: 'A request for Microsoft’s WebView2 setup program.',
  },
  {
    when: 'You click a link in Studio (a licence, a driver page, the docs)',
    who: 'You',
    host: 'Opens in your browser: the site you clicked',
    sent: 'Nothing from Dawnroom. Your browser makes the request.',
  },
];
---
<Base title="Privacy" description={`What ${PRODUCT_NAME} and this site do over the network, and what they never send.`}>
  <div class="wrap pt-10 md:pt-14">
    <header class="dl-head">
      <h1 class="display text-[2.8rem] leading-none sm:text-[3.6rem]">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-[38rem] text-[17px] text-muted">{PRODUCT_NAME} runs on your computer. Here is every connection it makes, and what this site stores.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="local-h" class="vision-why">
      <h2 id="local-h" class="dl-h2">On your computer</h2>
      <div class="vision-text">
        <p>Your prompts, your input images, your results and your history stay on your computer. The engine listens only on 127.0.0.1, so other devices on your network cannot reach it. The image runtime it starts (stable-diffusion.cpp) is given the same loopback address and a file path, never a web address to call.</p>
        <p>{PRODUCT_NAME} has no accounts, no analytics, no telemetry and no crash reporting. We searched the engine, Studio and its desktop shell, the installers and this site for tracking code and found none. Nothing is sent to us, because the app has no server of ours to send to.</p>
        <p>The MCP server and the CLI talk only to the engine on your own computer.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="net-h" class="dl-section">
      <h2 id="net-h" class="dl-h2">Connections</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[42rem] text-[15.5px] text-muted">These are the only times {PRODUCT_NAME} reaches out. All but one start with something you did. The hosts see your IP address, as any website does.</p>
      <dl class="dl-reqs">
        {connections.map((c) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{c.when}</dt>
            <dd>
              <strong class="font-medium">{c.host}.</strong> {c.sent} <span class="text-muted">Started by: {c.who}.</span>
            </dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[42rem] text-[15.5px] text-muted">To stop the daily update check, turn off “Update automatically” in Studio’s Settings. The {BIN} command line and the engine never check for updates by themselves.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="site-h" class="dl-section">
      <h2 id="site-h" class="dl-h2">This website</h2>
      <ul class="dash-list mt-4" role="list">
        <li>It loads no third-party scripts, fonts, embeds or analytics. Fonts and images come from this site.</li>
        <li>It sets no cookies.</li>
        <li>It stores two things in your browser’s localStorage, and sends neither anywhere: <code>dawnroom.hardware</code>, the graphics card and memory size you picked for the “Will it run on my machine?” check, and <code>dawnroom.intro</code>, which only records that the opening animation has played.</li>
        <li>The hardware check reads your browser’s graphics card name and user-agent text on your device, to guess your card. It does not send them. Clear them with “Change” on the check, or by clearing site data.</li>
        <li>The site is hosted by Vercel, which, like any host, keeps ordinary server logs of requests such as your IP address and the page you asked for. The site’s own code adds no tracking on top of that.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="own-h" class="dl-section">
      <h2 id="own-h" class="dl-h2">Models you add yourself</h2>
      <div class="vision-text">
        <p>A model you pull from Hugging Face, or a custom one you add, comes from a third party and is not reviewed by us. Its host has its own privacy policy. Models that ask you to accept a licence send nothing when you accept: the choice is saved in a file on your computer.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
